components.responsibility:
Get-W001RootShape classes -Root as one of four shapes:
- local-letter: matches ^[A-Za-z]:\\?$ and DriveInfo.DriveType is not Network;
- network-letter;
- unc;
- folder.

On a local-letter root, W-001 keeps every existing check (wcifs-layer-store precaution on, CheckPanelAgrees, the oracle, the checker controls) and adds four:
- report.outcome is 'completed';
- report.coverage is not null and window.CoveragePanel.visible is true;
- reasonCodeMismatches is 0;
- the 'refused-another-code' count is 0.
On a network-letter root, coverage is recorded when present but not required, because Q-003 is open.

The wait goes from 1200 s to 3600 s.

The record adds:
- outcome;
- coverage: Get-CountsOnly(report.coverage), meaning every number, boolean and null at any depth, with strings dropped. It also carries panelTop, textsHeight and textsOffset (rounded integers or null, from window.CoveragePanel.top and OutcomeTexts.actualHeight / verticalOffset), kept as data for Q-002 with no check on them;
- reasonCodeMismatches;
- oracle.refusedAnotherCode.
Nothing compares unseen with the $MFT figure. Q-001 is open and lesson #872 says the C:\ shape is unmeasured; the record's figures will answer it.

Get-ProofRecordPath gives docs/proof-runs/w001-<lower-case letter>-drive.json for both letter shapes, and artifacts/w001-run.json for unc and folder.

Write order: the record is written as soon as the finished run is judged. Before scanning, a letter run without -Stopped or -Force throws if its file already holds a 'stopped' part.

This runs only after the finished run has a report with status Completed. Otherwise the case is already FAILED, and no stopped part is written.

The checker controls stay planted. The stopped run uses stop mode with FSA_HOOK_ROWS=1 and FSA_HOOK_AT_FOLDERS = max(1, floor(finished core.folders / 2)), and waits 3600 s.

Read-ActedLine takes the folder count from ' folders=(\d+) ', the sizing state from ' sized=(\S+) ' and the time from ' ms=(\d+) (?:utc|sincearmed)='. The leading spaces matter: they keep 'atfolders=' from being read as the count, and they cover the armed form as well. A run counts as partial only when it is Cancelled with sized '-'. Otherwise the case retries with n halved, up to 3 attempts, and then ends inconclusive.

CheckPanelAgrees runs on the stopped run, then Compare-StoppedRows. Rows are keyed by path, OrdinalIgnoreCase. Folder times come through a $timesOf parameter. Its default lists the parent folder and reads the creation and last-write times from the find data, without opening the folder. Each stopped row gets one class:
- code 995: aborted;
- path absent from the finished tab, folder created or written after the finished run started: newSinceFinished;
- path absent, code 5: notInFinished;
- path absent, code not 5: otherCodeDiffers;
- path present, kind or code different, either code not 5: otherCodeDiffers;
- path present, both codes 5, kind different: codeChanged.

Get-StoppedVerdict:
- failed when aborted, notInFinished or codeChanged is above 0;
- inconclusive when otherCodeDiffers is above 0, or no run was partial;
- held otherwise.
newSinceFinished is only tallied.

The same file is rewritten with a 'stopped' part: status, outcome, atFolders, foldersAtStop, sizedAtStop (null for '-'), attempts, folders, rows, notInFinished, newSinceFinished, otherCodeDiffers, codeChanged, aborted and verdict. The rewrite happens in a finally, so a timeout or a throw still writes verdict 'failed'. Offending paths are printed to the console only.

The three '# settled by SL-003' entries the engine already appended (.taad/fitness.yaml:1495-1524) are this design's architecture_rules, word for word. The builder does not add them again.

The builder:
- deletes the SL-107 entry 'the committed whole-C:\ record carries counts, codes and reasons, never a path' (from line 1296), whose files is .taad/slices/SL-089/c-drive-run.json;
- in eng/rules-harness/plants.json, sets awaiting_file to { 'a committed proof-run record carries counts, codes and reasons, never a path': 'docs/proof-runs/w001-c-drive.json' };
- removes rows S83, S84, S85, S86 and P36, and adds five rows with new unused ids, the same texts, new-file at docs/proof-runs/w001-c-drive.json under the new rule name (xunit quiet; fitness fire for the four S rows and quiet for the P row);
- adds two rows for 'the window harness neither reads nor writes TAAD's slice records': one inserting a statement naming .taad\slices\X into WindowCases.ps1 (fitness fire), one naming docs\proof-runs (quiet);
- updates the wording of plants.json line 2 and of harness.py's load_awaiting docstring (line 594) to name the new path.
None of RuleCases C-006 to C-014 reads S83-S86 or P36, so none is retired.

A new W001ProofTests.cs loads functions from WindowCases.ps1's parse, as W001OracleTests does. It covers:
- Compare-StoppedRows (with a stubbed $timesOf), all six classes, and Get-StoppedVerdict;
- Read-ActedLine on the spike's exact progress line ('acted mode=stop atfolders=15151 folders=15202 sized=- current=X:\b148\s026 ms=2289 utc=...' gives 15202, '-' and 2289) and on the armed form;
- the partial rule;
- Get-ReasonCodeMismatches;
- Get-RecordByCode with a 995 row, after which Write-W001Record writes and does not throw;
- Get-CountsOnly on a coverage object that holds a remainder text;
- Get-W001RootShape and Get-ProofRecordPath;
- every -Network and -Link ValidateSet value and every fixed label, each in the writer's allowed set;
- the $ProofCases filter out of All;
- Get-HydrationTally.
W001OracleTests and its corpus gain the 'held' plant and the 'refused-another-code' row.

contracts.error_cases:
Throws:
- no -Root, or a -Root that is not a folder;
- -Stopped or -Force with another case;
- a letter run without -Stopped or -Force whose record already holds a 'stopped' part (before scanning).

INCONCLUSIVE (exit 3):
- elevated;
- the checker controls misbehaved;
- the stopped run was never partial in 3 attempts, or otherCodeDiffers is above 0.

FAILED (exit 1):
- the finished run timed out at 3600 s: no record;
- on a local letter, outcome not 'completed', null coverage or a hidden panel, reasonCodeMismatches above 0, refused-another-code above 0, or a leak: the finished part is written with verdict 'failed';
- the stopped run is aborted, or notInFinished or codeChanged is above 0, or it timed out or threw: stopped.verdict 'failed', written in a finally.

NOT RUN (exit 2): without -IncludeCloud.

INCONCLUSIVE:
- the provider was not READY;
- onlineOnlyBefore is 0.

FAILED:
- hydrated is above 0;
- dataFetches is above 0;
- a rig root is still registered, or its folder is left, after teardown;
- the app timed out at 120 s.

NOT RUN (exit 2): without -IncludeNetwork.

INCONCLUSIVE:
- the rig never served;
- the hold, a's refusal or b's failure came after the Stop;
- an answer other than 'cut', or the marker refused after the hook's 60 s deadline;
- the scan ended before the Stop.

FAILED:
- cutFolderRows is above 0;
- no timing could be read;
- a mapping is left;
- the app timed out.

The record is written in a finally whatever the ending.

contracts.notes:
W-001 keeps every existing key, and the change is additive only. It adds:
- outcome;
- coverage{counts-only copy of report.coverage, panelTop, textsHeight, textsOffset};
- reasonCodeMismatches;
- oracle.refusedAnotherCode;
- with -Stopped: stopped{status, outcome, atFolders, foldersAtStop, sizedAtStop, attempts, folders, rows, notInFinished, newSinceFinished, otherCodeDiffers, codeChanged, aborted, verdict}.

key_decisions.decision:
The record guard moves to the SL-003 entries the engine has already appended:
- the SL-107 entry is deleted, not renamed;
- awaiting_file is re-keyed to the new rule name and docs/proof-runs/w001-c-drive.json;
- S83-S86 and P36 are removed;
- the same five texts are re-planted at docs/proof-runs/w001-c-drive.json under new ids;
- the WindowCases.ps1 rule gets one fire plant and one quiet plant.

Compare-StoppedRows fails only on the shapes a cut folder leaves:
- 995 rows;
- code-5 rows the finished tab lacks, for folders that existed before the finished run;
- code-5 rows whose kind changed.
Rows created or written after the finished run started are tallied. Any difference where either code is not 5 makes the verdict inconclusive.

Counts only, enforced by the callers:
- Write-W001Record stays strict and throws;
- Get-RecordByCode writes a null reason wherever the reason holds '/' or '\';
- coverage is copied by Get-CountsOnly, which drops strings;
- a Fact pins every label into the allowed set.

proposals.note:
The only proposal, taken as the core.

Kept:
- the case functions and their record shapes;
- the -Stopped mechanism, which the spike measured as go;
- the M1 and M2 classes;
- the writer's strictness and the byCode filtering;
- the script retirements.

Changed at the seams after reading the tree:
- the engine-appended SL-003 fitness entries are adopted, and SL-107's entry is deleted rather than renamed;
- the five plant rows are re-planted at docs/proof-runs rather than dropped;
- W-003's rig judgement uses N-005's rule for t and u rather than a fixed count of 2 rows;
- Get-W001Verdict keeps its signature;
- coverage is copied by a walk that drops strings;
- coverage is required on local letters only (Q-003 is open).

Its over_engineering_flag was honoured, and this design trims further.
